    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d676">

                <pb facs="0654" n="564" xml:id="pg564"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/3037</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Russia</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Francis</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-10-31T15:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 31,
                                1918, 3 p.m.</hi></date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>331. Your 510, October 23, 6 p.m., under consideration. For your confidential
                    information: command of forces in northern Russia was assigned to the British by
                    decision of War Council at Versailles. Any change would require consideration by
                    the Council. War Department would probably agree to control of American troops
                    by Russian only if officer selected were of definitely approved capacity.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Lansing</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
